{% doc %}
  The most recently closed tickets the viewer is allowed to see.

  A separate query from the queue, with its own small cap. Closed tickets
  are the one unbounded part of a support instance: the queue has as many
  open tickets as the team is behind by, and as many closed ones as it has
  ever had. Folding them into the queue's 500 would let a year of finished
  work crowd out this morning's.

  The board's Closed column is the only screen that asks for these, it
  starts collapsed, and it says so when it is showing a capped slice.

  @param {object} agent - The viewing agent; admins see every department
  @param {array} statuses - Every status, to work out which ones are closed
  @param {number} [limit] - Defaults to 50
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign limit = limit | default: 50

  assign closed_status_ids = []
  for status in statuses
    if status.kind == 'closed'
      assign closed_status_ids = closed_status_ids | array_add: status.id
    endif
  endfor

  if closed_status_ids == empty
    return empty
  endif

  assign department_ids = null
  unless agent.role == 'admin'
    assign department_ids = agent.department_ids
  endunless

  comment
    Most recently closed first. closed_at is written as YYYY-MM-DD
    HH:MM:SS, so a plain descending sort is chronological.
  endcomment
  assign sort = { "properties": { "name": "closed_at", "order": "DESC" } }
  graphql result = 'modules/support/tickets/search', status_ids: closed_status_ids, department_ids: department_ids, sort: sort, limit: limit, page: 1, id: null, number: null, department_id: null, status_id: null, contact_id: null, assignee_id: null, priority: null, query: null

  return result.records.results
%}
